Bro, crystal clear now. 👍

And yes — I would keep the architecture essentially as-is. After reviewing the whole 60-point version again, I don't see unnecessary architecture that should be removed. Some sections may look detailed, but they are there because a future coding LLM needs to understand why the pieces exist and how they interact. Removing them could create ambiguity later.

The only corrections I would make are:

1. Provider is the source of truth for usage, quota, allowance, reset and billing wherever the provider exposes those values.


2. CNS does not independently calculate provider consumption or actual cost when provider data exists.


3. Mandatory CNS spending limits are NOT part of the current design. They remain a future decision after we observe real usage/cost.


4. Entitlement remains because it means permission/access, while allowance means available usage. They are different concepts.


5. Subscription and API remain separate access paths.


6. Everything remains under the future Universal Model Bus.


7. The existing Local LLM Path remains untouched.



Here is the fresh final version I would save.


