67. FINAL LOCKED RULES

1. Paid and Local are sibling execution paths.

2. Neither path becomes CNS itself.

3. Both eventually connect through the Universal Model Bus.

4. API access and Subscription access remain separate.

5. Subscription access must use officially supported provider mechanisms.

6. Provider-reported usage is the source of truth.

7. Provider-reported quota/allowance is the source of truth.

8. Provider-reported reset information is the source of truth.

9. Provider-reported actual cost is the source of truth when available.

10. CNS does not invent or silently calculate provider usage when
    authoritative provider data exists.

11. CNS estimates must always be clearly labelled as estimates.

12. CNS does not currently impose mandatory spending limits.

13. Spending restrictions are a FUTURE decision after observing
    real-world usage and cost.

14. CNS must preserve workflow continuity when a preferred paid
    model becomes unavailable.

15. Model switching must never destroy CNS memory, state or identity.

16. Provider-specific logic belongs inside adapters.

17. Provider credentials must remain securely managed.

18. Entitlement, allowance, usage, credits and billing are distinct
    concepts.

19. Model identity and execution access are distinct concepts.

20. Account identity and provider identity are distinct concepts.

21. The architecture must allow future providers and future access
    mechanisms without redesigning CNS Core.


